{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Employee Aisha Bello (E028, Payroll Specialist, Finance) received a jury summons for the week of 2027-01-11 and asks whether Fernhollow pays for jury duty or whether it must be taken as PTO, and whether the summons must be sent to anyone. Policy POL-PTO-01 (PTO) and POL-OFF-02 (leaves of absence) were checked and do not mention jury duty. Please advise on jury duty pay and the notification process."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Hi Aisha,\n\nI checked our policies, and none of them covers jury duty. The PTO policy (POL-PTO-01) covers booking time off, but it doesn't say whether jury service is paid or whether it has to be taken as PTO. The leave policy (POL-OFF-02) doesn't cover it either. I can't answer from general knowledge, so I've passed your question to the HR team with the details: your jury summons for the week of 11 January 2027, and your questions about pay and whether the summons needs to go to anyone. HR will reply to you directly.\n\nIn the meantime, please keep the summons. If it asks for a response by a certain date, don't let that deadline pass.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-PTO-01",
  "POL-OFF-02"
 ]
}
